## 434c Mathematical Review: PASS

The revised display and expression key both give:

```latex
\frac{x^2-7x+19}{x^2-x+1}
```

The displayed restriction remains x!=-1, for real x.

```text
(x-2)^3+27
= ((x-2)+3)((x-2)^2-3(x-2)+9)
= (x+1)(x^2-7x+19).

(x+1)(x^2-7x+19)
= x^3-6x^2+12x+19
= (x-2)^3+27.

x^3+1=(x+1)(x^2-x+1).
```

Canceling x+1 on the original domain gives the revised expression exactly.
The residual denominator is x^2-x+1=(x-1/2)^2+3/4>0 for every real x. Thus -1 is the sole excluded real input of the original fraction, and cancellation must not restore it.
No residual common polynomial factor remains: numerator minus denominator is -6x+18, whose only root 3 is not a denominator root (the denominator there is 7).
Checks at permitted inputs x=0 and x=2 give 19 and 3 respectively in both the original and revised expression.
The observed expected array has one pure LaTeX expression, label c), judge expression, and no explanation/domain prose in the key.

This resolves ANS-N21-434c-01 only on the new recovery candidate. Its false factorization and bad key on the FIRST candidate remain historical facts.

